🚨 Mandatory reading! A very pragmatic and down-to-earth perspective on the current state of diffusion large language models by the LLaDA lead Junbo Zhao.

@JunboZhao118809: "Some Theoretical and Practical Thoughts on Diffusion Language Models."

The linked article provides a retrospective on the past year of work on diffusion language models, from LLaDA-MoE to LLaDA 2.2, and discusses what it would take for diffusion LLMs to become an independent scaling paradigm.

Also: Anyone can code in Python, but only a few people know how to write good Python code. Anyone can build an abstraction, but only a few know how to create a simple, scalable, and intuitive one.

@vboykis: "Thank you. While it’s true that there are a lot of non-code aspects to being a good programmer, getting good at 'just' writing code is not easy."

The software development profession is currently experiencing upheaval due to the AI revolution, but the skill of writing high-quality code remains a challenging and valuable ability.
